{"title":"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In how many distinct ways can a rectangular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201f44665542b2727117f2a75cdb4fcc85f6d2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times 17$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> grid be tiled with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> non-overlapping <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/d/0ddb906eeaf8722fe7a6f2cdb30d292557d97967.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> rectangular tiles? \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In both solutions we consider the grid to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> rows and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> columns.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>There are either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> vertical tiles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> vertical and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> horizontal, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> vertical and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> horizontal, etc. \nThe horizontal tiles always have to form blocks <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5343f2d9e22816e8de24262565ff2937695b2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>If we now consider tilings that consist of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> vertical tiles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> blocks of three horizontal tiles, it is clear that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e787d59adc63135872a5c4617ca555d7485a0e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b \\choose b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"53\" height=\"27\" /> such tilings. Hence we get that the total number of tilings in our case is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/5/9a58d8a8d4d7078e50681d33efdc946240d9632d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{17!}{17!}+\\dfrac{15!}{14!}+\\dfrac{13!}{11!\\cdot 2!}+\\dfrac{11!}{8!\\cdot 3!}+\\dfrac{9!}{5!\\cdot 4!}+\\dfrac{7!}{2!\\cdot 5!}\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>It isn't that such a pain to compute, so we do:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/889ef5fe36370dac14bb883ea5e8a7264d6f5a8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1+15+78+165+126+21=\\boxed{406}\\]\" width=\"291\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/f/82f4341a1efbe1a890de160de023b4e4b84ef444.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> be the number of ways to tile a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2dd3c581fc74f59062d697995615bb5cfcbc0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times n$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> rectangle.\n</p><p>Obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b08da992d6850c6a26f2aa1a9d7967e86680dcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_0=T_1=T_2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"135\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Consider a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/2/ec2dd3c581fc74f59062d697995615bb5cfcbc0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\times n$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> rectangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811f76ab716762dc2652ba611378a1816b671893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />. Take a look at the tile that contains the upper right corner. It can be either vertical or horizontal. If it is vertical, we still need to tile the remaining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/d/4bdca93962a2beaffc172ca394e04fe05bd74ffd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> columns. If it is horizontal, the other two cells in the rightmost column must be covered by horizontal tiles as well. We are then left with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/31503c8c86ff405ea9ae2dd6285eecb04550cb97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n-3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" /> columns to tile.\n</p><p>This gives us the recurrence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/9/90902819d82818caf0c7f6ba8e0c20f7c9f952cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T_n = T_{n-1} + T_{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"138\" height=\"15\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/1/811f76ab716762dc2652ba611378a1816b671893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Using it we can now compute:\n</p>\n<pre>  n | T(n)\n------------\n  3 |   2\n  4 |   3\n  5 |   4\n  6 |   6\n  7 |   9\n  8 |  13\n  9 |  19\n 10 |  28\n 11 |  41\n 12 |  60\n 13 |  88\n 14 | 129\n 15 | 189\n 16 | 277\n 17 | 406\n</pre>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST\">2007 Alabama ARML TST</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems\">(Problems)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_Alabama_ARML_TST_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2007 Alabama ARML TST Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017213546\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 193/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1384/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 217/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4418/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.823      1 Template:ARML_box\n100.00%    6.823      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6852:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017213546 and revision id 29765. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}